# placetel.dadl — Placetel REST API v2 for ToolMesh
# Placetel is a German cloud telephone system (hosted PBX). Its REST API v2
# covers the call log, click-to-dial, call detail records, recordings,
# contacts, SMS, fax, numbers, call routing (forwards, groups, IVR, queues,
# routing plans), SIP users, users, prompts, the call center, CTI call
# control of desk phones, phone provisioning, call event webhooks, and the
# Microsoft Teams and Webex integrations.
#
# Domain Notes for LLM consumers:
# - SOURCE: written from the official OpenAPI 2.0 document
#   (https://api.placetel.de/v2/swagger_doc, "Placetel API" 2.0.0, read
#   2026-11-07). The read tools were verified against a live account on
#   2026-11-09 (response shapes, filters, number formats, paging, error
#   codes, redaction); contacts, prompts, routing objects, routing plans,
#   groups and number profiles were also created, updated and deleted.
#   Calls, SMS, fax, SIP users, users, short codes (only the validation was
#   seen), CTI, call center, recordings, Teams, Webex and the partner
#   customer endpoints were not exercised live; where the document leaves
#   their behavior open (partial PUT updates, array query parameters) the
#   tool descriptions say so. Verified for contacts, routings, routing plans
#   and groups: PUT changes only the fields sent.
# - AUTH: one API key from the web portal (Integrations > Web API,
#   https://web.placetel.de/integrations/web_api), sent as
#   "Authorization: Bearer <key>". An existing API v1 key also works for v2.
#   Tokens carry scopes: a regular account token reached every endpoint of
#   the booked products, while the partner customer endpoints answered 403
#   'Access to this resource requires scope "read:customers"'. Missing
#   header -> 401 {"error":"missing_bearer_token"}, unknown or revoked key
#   -> 401 {"error":"inactive_token"}.
# - BASE URL: https://api.placetel.de/v2 (SaaS, one global endpoint). Request
#   and response bodies are JSON.
# - PAGINATION: page (starting at 1) and per_page (API default 25, max 100;
#   list_call_detail_records allows 500). Lists return a plain JSON array
#   without envelope, total or has_more flag: a page with fewer items than
#   per_page is the last one. The API notes that not every endpoint honors
#   per_page; a value above the maximum is rejected with 400 "per_page does
#   not have a valid value". This file sends per_page=100 and exposes paging
#   to the caller (behavior expose), because ToolMesh cannot detect the last
#   page of a bare array in auto mode. The call log, call detail records and
#   call center calls are per day: one request series per date.
# - RATE LIMIT: token bucket with a burst allowance. Every response carries
#   RateLimit-Remaining (requests left right now) and RateLimit-Reset (seconds
#   until the next token). Over the limit -> 429 with Retry-After (seconds).
#   Prefer server-side filters over paging through everything.
# - ERRORS: {"error": "<code or message>", "status": <http status>,
#   "request_id": "<uuid>"}. Seen: missing_bearer_token and inactive_token
#   (401), route_not_found (404), "404 not found" for unknown IDs and
#   unbooked products, validation failures as 400 with a readable message.
#   Some product errors are German text.
# - EMPTY OR UNKNOWN FILTERS (verified): an empty string is sent as a real
#   filter value and returns an empty list (filter[type]="",
#   filter[from_number]="", filter[number]=""), and an unknown enum value
#   such as filter[type]="outgoing" also returns an empty list instead of
#   400. Only some parameters are validated (order -> 400). Omit filters
#   you do not use, and do not read an empty result after a filter as proof
#   that nothing exists.
# - NO IDEMPOTENCY KEYS: POST and PATCH calls (initiate_call, send_sms,
#   send_fax, dial_cti_number, ...) are never retried automatically. After a
#   timeout the call may still have been placed or the SMS sent: check
#   (list_calls, list_call_detail_records, list_faxes) before sending again.
#   create_subscription (a PUT) is excluded from retries for the same reason.
# - PHONE NUMBERS (verified live): number fields and filters use German
#   national format without spaces, exactly as in Number.number
#   ("02211234567"). filter[number], filter[from_number], filter[to_number]
#   and the number form of number_or_id only match that format: the E.164
#   form ("+492211234567") and numonly find nothing or answer 404. Number
#   objects also carry e164, prefix (area code, "0221") and numonly.
#   CONTACTS ARE DIFFERENT: they store valid German numbers in E.164
#   ("+492211234567") whatever format was sent, so their exact filters
#   (filter[phone], filter[mobile], ...) need E.164, while search[number]
#   normalizes and finds any complete form of a valid number.
# - SIPUID: a SIP user (phone extension) is addressed as
#   "<username>@<sip domain>", e.g. "7771234567@fpbx.de". Forward targets and
#   initiate_call accept a sipuid or an external phone number.
# - IDS: numeric IDs, except subscriptions ("sub-..."). Routings are
#   addressed by phone number OR routing ID (number_or_id). A Number links to
#   its routing via routing_id; a SIP user has routing_plan_id (fallback when
#   busy or unanswered).
# - TIMESTAMPS: ISO 8601 with offset in German local time
#   ("2026-11-07T11:42:47.000+01:00"). Date filters are YYYY-MM-DD.
# - CALL DATA: list_calls is the log of INCOMING calls (type accepted, missed,
#   voicemail or blocked; voicemails carry file_url; to_number is the full
#   Number object of the dialed number). Outgoing calls only show up in
#   list_call_detail_records (billing records with amount, length, from, to,
#   oldest first). Recordings exist only with call recording booked.
# - ROUTING MODEL: incoming call -> Number -> routing object (one per number)
#   with exactly one behavior: forward (ordered destination steps, each
#   {targets[], ringing_time}), group (ring a group), plan (a routing plan),
#   ivr (voice menu: prompt plus items 1-9 pointing at other routing
#   objects), queue (call center queue), api (ask an external API, with retry
#   count and backup plan) or ai (Placetel AI; returned, not writable here).
#   Every routing object also has mailbox (voicemail), notification (e-mail),
#   time_settings (active weekdays, hours, holidays), a custom caller ID and
#   music on hold. Routing plans order several routing objects by priority;
#   simulate_routing_plan shows which one answers at a given time. A routing
#   object added to a plan belongs to it: deleting the plan deleted that
#   routing object too (verified). Number profiles are saved alternative
#   configurations of a number; one is active. The active profile "Standard"
#   is the number's own routing object (profile id = Number.routing_id), so
#   deleting it would remove the number's routing.
# - PUT ON ROUTINGS (verified): update_routing changes only the objects sent;
#   name, forward, time_settings and mailbox stay as they are when omitted.
#   ringing_time accepts only the listed values (33 -> 400).
# - USERS vs SIP USERS: a user ("webuser": web portal login, main account or
#   subuser) owns SIP users (phone extensions with sipuid, did = internal
#   extension number, callerid). Groups contain SIP users (member_ids).
#   Provisionings bind a physical phone (MAC address, model from
#   list_devices) to SIP users (lines) and function keys.
# - SECRETS: SIP user objects carry the SIP password (single GET and create)
#   and the hotdesk PIN; Webex fax settings carry the fax PIN. This file masks
#   them with response.redact wherever they appear, because SIP credentials
#   enable toll fraud. Read them in the web portal. Setting hotdesk_pin or
#   faxpin still works.
# - FILES IN: send_fax (PDF), create_prompt/update_prompt (audio) and
#   update_user (avatar) take a base64 data URI ("data:application/pdf;
#   base64,..."). In ToolMesh pass a blob handle with the #dataurl fragment
#   (tm-blob://<id>#dataurl after upload_file) so the bytes never pass
#   through the model. FILES OUT: voicemail file_url, recording file, fax
#   file and report, and prompt file are URLs. Prompt file URLs are signed
#   and expire after about 5 minutes (verified); fetch the record again for
#   a fresh one.
# - QUERY ARRAYS: array filters (call center queue_ids, recordings direction,
#   CTI params) are declared with the "[]" key suffix and take ONE value per
#   call, because ToolMesh sends one value per query key.
# - CTI: call control of a desk phone provisioned through Placetel, addressed
#   by its MAC address (mac of list_provisionings). line is the account line
#   on the phone, call_id the phone-side integer call ID. These are not the
#   sha256 call_id values of webhook events.
# - WEBHOOKS: create_subscription registers a URL for call events (incoming,
#   outgoing, accepted, hungup, phone = CTI). Per Placetel's Notify API
#   documentation the events arrive as form-encoded POSTs with event
#   (IncomingCall, OutgoingCall, CallAccepted, HungUp), call_id (sha256 hex),
#   from, to and direction, signed in X-PLACETEL-SIGNATURE (HMAC-SHA256) once
#   a shared secret is set in the portal's external API settings.
# - PRODUCT-DEPENDENT AREAS: call center, Microsoft Teams direct routing,
#   Webex (Webex Calling wholesale), Placetel AI, SIM cards (Placetel Mobile)
#   and customers (partner accounts) only work when booked. Observed without
#   the product: call center and recordings answer 404 "404 not found",
#   Webex answers 403 "Not available for your product", Microsoft Teams
#   answers 403 until the Teams integration is enabled for API access, and
#   the customer endpoints need the read:customers scope. Number activation
#   can be charged. Placetel AI Pro (voice agents, their tools and
#   conversation transcripts) is a separate product with its own API and
#   its own MCP server; it is not covered here.
# - VOCABULARY: "routing" = routing object of a number; "sip user" = phone
#   extension; "webuser" = user; "did" = INTERNAL extension number, not an
#   external number; "prompt" = announcement audio; "short code" = star code
#   dialed on the phone that triggers an action. Spellings such as "dail_in",
#   "dail_out" and "behaviour" are the API's own.

spec: "https://dadl.ai/spec/dadl-spec-v0.2.md"
requires:
  features: [redact]
credits:
  - "Dunkel Cloud GmbH -- maintainer"
source_name: "Placetel REST API v2"
source_url: https://api.placetel.de/v2/docs/
date: "2026-11-09"

# ─── Reusable fragments (underscore keys are ignored by ToolMesh) ────────────
_shared:
  page_param: &p-page
    type: integer
    in: query
    default: 1
    description: "Page number, starting at 1. The result is a plain array; a page shorter than per_page is the last one."
  per_page_param: &p-per-page
    type: integer
    in: query
    default: 100
    description: "Items per page, 1-100 (API default 25); larger values are rejected with 400."
  updated_gte_param: &p-updated-gte
    type: string
    in: query
    description: "Only records updated at or after this ISO 8601 date-time (incremental sync)."
  updated_lte_param: &p-updated-lte
    type: string
    in: query
    description: "Only records updated at or before this ISO 8601 date-time."
  order_param: &p-order
    type: string
    in: query
    description: "Sort order by time: desc (newest first, API default) or asc."
  # SIP credentials in responses (toll-fraud risk) are masked everywhere.
  redact_sip_user: &redact-sip-user
    - "$.password"
    - "$.hotdesk_pin"
  redact_sip_user_list: &redact-sip-user-list
    - "$[*].password"
    - "$[*].hotdesk_pin"
  redact_group: &redact-group
    - "$.members[*].password"
    - "$.members[*].hotdesk_pin"
  redact_group_list: &redact-group-list
    - "$[*].members[*].password"
    - "$[*].members[*].hotdesk_pin"
  redact_sim_card: &redact-sim-card
    - "$.sip_user.password"
    - "$.sip_user.hotdesk_pin"
  redact_sim_card_list: &redact-sim-card-list
    - "$[*].sip_user.password"
    - "$[*].sip_user.hotdesk_pin"
  redact_fax_settings: &redact-fax-settings
    - "$.faxpin"
  # Shared body params of create_routing and update_routing.
  routing_forward: &p-routing-forward
    type: object
    in: body
    description: "Forward behavior: {destinations: [{targets: [sipuid or external number, ...], ringing_time: 10-120 s (default 60)}], behaviour: ringing|mailbox|prompt_and_disconnect|prompt_and_ringing, prompt_id}. Destinations are tried in order; all targets of one step ring at once. behaviour is what happens when nobody answers (or before ringing, for the prompt_* values)."
  routing_group: &p-routing-group
    type: object
    in: body
    description: "Group behavior: {id: group ID (required), group_ringing_time: 10|15|20|25|30|40|60|90|120 (default 40), backup_behaviour: ringing|mailbox|prompt_and_disconnect|prompt_and_ringing, backup_routing_object_id}."
  routing_ivr: &p-routing-ivr
    type: object
    in: body
    description: "IVR (voice menu) behavior: {prompt_id: menu announcement, item_1_id ... item_9_id: routing object ID per key, catchall_routing_object_id: routing object for no or invalid input}."
  routing_queue: &p-routing-queue
    type: object
    in: body
    description: "Call center queue behavior: {id: queue ID from list_call_center_queues}."
  routing_api: &p-routing-api
    type: object
    in: body
    description: "External API behavior (Placetel asks your API how to route): {max_retries (required), backup_routing_plan_id, prompt_id}."
  routing_mailbox: &p-routing-mailbox
    type: object
    in: body
    description: "Voicemail: {active: boolean, greeting_id: prompt ID of the greeting, mp3: boolean (send recordings as MP3)}."
  routing_notification: &p-routing-notification
    type: object
    in: body
    description: "E-mail notification: {salutation, email, type: none|all|voicemail|missed, receiver: global|local}."
  routing_time_settings: &p-routing-time-settings
    type: object
    in: body
    description: "When this routing object is active: {enabled, mon, tue, wed, thu, fri, sat, sun (booleans), nationwide_holidays (active on nationwide German holidays), extended_time_settings}. With extended_time_settings=false use time_from/time_to ('08:00:00', '19:59:59'); with true use time_ranges ('08:30:00-13:29:59,14:30:00-17:59:59'), additional_dates (day.month list without year, '24.12,31.12') and additional_holidays (new_year, good_friday, easter, easter_monday, labor_day, ascension_day, whitmonday, day_of_german_unity, christmas, epiphany, corpus_christi, assumption_day, reformation_day, all_saints_day, repentance_day). Setting additional_dates or additional_holidays makes nationwide_holidays ignored."
  routing_callerid: &p-routing-callerid
    type: object
    in: body
    description: "Caller ID shown on forwarded calls: {callerid_enabled, callerid_name, callerid_number}. Note: responses name this object custom_caller_id with fields enabled, name, number."
  routing_moh: &p-routing-moh
    type: boolean
    in: body
    description: "Play music on hold while the caller waits."
  routing_notify_api: &p-routing-notify-api
    type: boolean
    in: body
    description: "Send call events of this routing to the external API (webhook) configuration."

backend:
  name: placetel
  type: rest
  version: "1.0"
  base_url: https://api.placetel.de/v2
  description: >
    Placetel REST API v2 — German cloud telephone system (hosted PBX): call
    log and voicemails, click-to-dial, call detail records, call recordings,
    contacts and caller lookup, SMS and fax, phone numbers and number
    profiles, call routing (forwards, ring groups, IVR menus, call center
    queues, routing plans, time settings), SIP users and short codes, users
    and permissions, announcements (text-to-speech prompts), call center
    agents and queues, CTI call control of desk phones, phone provisioning,
    call event webhooks, Microsoft Teams direct routing and Webex Calling.

  coverage:
    endpoints: 127
    total_endpoints: 127
    percentage: 100
    focus: >
      Placetel REST API v2: calls (call log, voicemails, click-to-dial, call
      detail records, recordings), CTI call control (answer, hold, transfer,
      conference, DTMF), routing (forwards, ring groups, IVR menus, queues,
      routing plans, time settings, number profiles), SIP users (extensions,
      short codes, hotdesking), contacts, numbers, SMS, fax, prompts, call
      center, users, phone provisioning, webhooks, Microsoft Teams, Webex.
    missing: >
      Every endpoint of the published document is declared. Limits: array
      query filters take one value per call (call center queue_ids,
      recordings direction, CTI config params); the ai routing behavior is
      returned but cannot be written; webhook callbacks themselves are
      delivered outside the REST API; SIP passwords, hotdesk PINs and fax
      PINs are masked in responses. Read tools and the write tools for
      contacts, prompts, routings, routing plans, groups and number profiles
      verified against a live account on 2026-11-09; calls, SMS, fax, SIP
      users, users, short codes, CTI, call center, recordings, Teams, Webex
      and customers not yet tested live. The allowed short code values are
      not documented.
    last_reviewed: "2026-11-09"

  setup:
    credential_steps:
      - "Sign in to the Placetel web portal at https://web.placetel.de."
      - "Open Integrations > Web API (https://web.placetel.de/integrations/web_api)."
      - "Create a new API token there, or copy the existing one (an API v1 key also works for v2). Store it right away."
      - "Partner accounts only: the customer endpoints need a token with the read:customers scope."
      - "Put the key into the ToolMesh .env as CREDENTIAL_PLACETEL_API_KEY and add the backends.yaml entry below."
      - "Restart ToolMesh and call placetel_health (or get_me): it must return your account with id and name."
    env_var: CREDENTIAL_PLACETEL_API_KEY
    backends_yaml: |
      - name: placetel
        transport: rest
        dadl: placetel.dadl
        url: "https://api.placetel.de/v2"
    required_scopes:
      - "A regular account token: it reaches every endpoint of the booked products"
    optional_scopes:
      - "read:customers (partner accounts: list_customers, get_customer; create_customer presumably needs a write scope, not verified)"
    docs_url: "https://api.placetel.de/v2/docs/"
    notes: >
      The key has full access to the account: it can place calls, send SMS
      and faxes, change routings, delete data and manage users. Restrict what
      agents may do with ToolMesh authorization on the access classes (read,
      write, admin, dangerous). Call center, Microsoft Teams, Webex, Placetel
      AI, SIM cards and the partner customer endpoints only answer when the
      product is booked; Microsoft Teams additionally has to be enabled for
      API access. The API is rate limited (token bucket; 429 with
      Retry-After).

  auth:
    type: bearer
    credential: placetel_api_key
    inject_into: header
    header_name: Authorization
    prefix: "Bearer "

  health:
    tool: get_me
    expect_path: "$.id"

  defaults:
    headers:
      Accept: application/json
    content_type: application/json
    pagination:
      strategy: page
      request:
        page_param: page
        limit_param: per_page
        limit_default: 100
      behavior: expose
      max_pages: 10
    errors:
      format: json
      message_path: "$.error"
      retry_on: [429, 502, 503, 504]
      terminal: [400, 401, 403, 404, 409, 422]
      rate_limit:
        header: RateLimit-Remaining
        retry_after_header: Retry-After
      retry_strategy:
        max_retries: 3
        backoff: exponential
        initial_delay: 2s
    response:
      result_path: "$"

  tools:
    # ── Account ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    get_me:
      method: GET
      path: /me
      access: read
      description: >
        The account behind the API key: {id, name, email, company,
        primary_sip_user_id, platform (product line, e.g. PROFI),
        rights_numbers (numbers this login may see), main_account_id,
        created_at, updated_at}. Cheapest call to check that the key works;
        used as the health check.
      pagination: none

    get_ai_status:
      method: GET
      path: /ai/status
      access: read
      description: >
        Status and usage of the account's Placetel AI integration: {status
        (e.g. active), minute_package, remaining_minutes, remaining_budget,
        total_cost (net AI cost of the last 7 days), currency, refreshed_at}.
        The budget figures are only present while the integration is active;
        otherwise only status is returned.
      pagination: none

    # ── Calls (call log, click-to-dial) ────────────────────────────────────

    list_calls:
      method: GET
      path: /calls
      access: read
      description: >
        Call log of INCOMING calls for ONE day (default today), newest first.
        For a period, call once per date. Each Call: {id, type (accepted |
        missed | voicemail | blocked), from_number (national format),
        to_number (the full Number object of the dialed number: id, number,
        e164, prefix, numonly, routing_id, site_id, ...), duration
        (seconds), file_url (audio of a voicemail, else null), contact (the
        matching contact or null), received_at, unread}. Number filters take
        the national format (02211234567); E.164 finds nothing. Omit unused
        filters: an empty or unknown filter value (e.g. filter[type]="" or
        "outgoing") silently returns an empty list. Outgoing calls are not in this log: use
        list_call_detail_records. Paged: plain array, increment page until a
        page has fewer than per_page items.
      params:
        "filter[date]":
          type: string
          in: query
          description: "Day as YYYY-MM-DD. Defaults to today."
        "filter[type]":
          type: string
          in: query
          description: "accepted, missed, voicemail or blocked. The combinations 'voicemail,missed' and 'missed,blocked,accepted' are accepted too."
        "filter[from_number]": { type: string, in: query, description: "Only calls from this caller number, national format as in from_number (e.g. 02211234567)." }
        "filter[to_number]": { type: string, in: query, description: "Only calls to this Placetel number, national format as in to_number.number; the E.164 form finds nothing." }
        order: *p-order
        page: *p-page
        per_page: *p-per-page

    get_call:
      method: GET
      path: /calls/{id}
      access: read
      description: "One call of the incoming call log by ID (same fields as list_calls)."
      params:
        id: { type: integer, in: path, required: true, description: "Call ID from list_calls." }
      pagination: none

    initiate_call:
      method: POST
      path: /calls
      access: write
      description: >
        Click-to-dial: Placetel rings the phone(s) registered for sipuid and,
        once answered there, connects to target. Returns the created Call.
        Not retried automatically (no idempotency key): after a timeout check
        before dialing again.
      params:
        sipuid: { type: string, in: body, required: true, description: "SIP user that places the call, e.g. 7771234567@fpbx.de (sipuid from list_sip_users)." }
        target: { type: string, in: body, required: true, description: "Number to call, e.g. 02211234567 or +492211234567." }
        from_name: { type: string, in: body, description: "Optional display name for the call." }
      pagination: none

    delete_call:
      method: DELETE
      path: /calls/{id}
      access: dangerous
      description: "Delete an entry of the incoming call log, e.g. a voicemail. Irreversible. Returns no body (204)."
      params:
        id: { type: integer, in: path, required: true, description: "Call ID." }
      pagination: none

    # ── Call detail records ────────────────────────────────────────────────

    list_call_detail_records:
      method: GET
      path: /call_detail_records
      access: read
      description: >
        Billing records (itemized call records) of ONE day, including
        outgoing calls and forwards: {amount (charge in the account
        currency), description (connection type label), from, to, length
        (seconds), answer_uri (who answered, null if nobody), received_at},
        oldest first. date is required; for a period call once per day. per_page goes up to 500
        here. Paged: plain array.
      params:
        date: { type: string, in: query, required: true, description: "Day as YYYY-MM-DD." }
        page: *p-page
        per_page:
          type: integer
          in: query
          default: 100
          description: "Items per page, 1-500 (API default 25)."

    # ── Recordings ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    list_recordings:
      method: GET
      path: /recordings
      access: read
      description: >
        Call recordings, newest first; without booked call recording the API
        answers 404 "404 not found". Each:
        {id, direction (e.g. in), from, to, duration (seconds), time, file
        (URL of the audio file), created_at, updated_at}. Paged: plain array.
      params:
        "filter[date]": { type: string, in: query, description: "Day as YYYY-MM-DD." }
        "filter[from]": { type: string, in: query, description: "Caller number." }
        "filter[to]": { type: string, in: query, description: "Called number." }
        "filter[direction][]": { type: string, in: query, description: "ONE direction as in the direction field, e.g. in or out (array filter, one value per call)." }
        order: *p-order
        page: *p-page
        per_page: *p-per-page

    get_recording:
      method: GET
      path: /recordings/{id}
      access: read
      description: "One call recording by ID, with the file URL of the audio."
      params:
        id: { type: integer, in: path, required: true, description: "Recording ID." }
      pagination: none

    delete_recording:
      method: DELETE
      path: /recordings/{id}
      access: dangerous
      description: "Delete a call recording and its audio. Irreversible. Returns no body (204)."
      params:
        id: { type: integer, in: path, required: true, description: "Recording ID." }
      pagination: none

    # ── Contacts (phone book, caller lookup, blocklist) ────────────────────

    list_contacts:
      method: GET
      path: /contacts
      access: read
      description: >
        Phone book contacts: {id, user_id, speeddial, first_name, last_name,
        email, email_work, company, address, address_work, phone, phone_work,
        mobile, mobile_work, fax, fax_work, facebook_url, linkedin_url,
        xing_url, twitter_account, blocked, color, tags, created_at,
        updated_at}. For caller lookup use search[number]: it normalizes, so
        02211234567, +492211234567 and 2211234567 all find the contact
        (partial numbers do not). Valid German numbers are stored in E.164,
        so the exact filters filter[phone], filter[mobile] etc. need the
        +49 form. All filters are exact matches (no prefix search).
        Contacts with blocked=true form the account's blocklist. Paged:
        plain array.
      params:
        "search[number]": { type: string, in: query, description: "Find contacts by a complete phone number in any format (national, +49, without leading 0); searches all number fields." }
        "filter[first_name]": { type: string, in: query }
        "filter[last_name]": { type: string, in: query }
        "filter[company]": { type: string, in: query }
        "filter[email]": { type: string, in: query }
        "filter[email_work]": { type: string, in: query }
        "filter[phone]": { type: string, in: query, description: "Exact match on the stored value: E.164 for valid numbers, e.g. +492211234567." }
        "filter[phone_work]": { type: string, in: query, description: "Exact match on the stored value: E.164 for valid numbers, e.g. +492211234567." }
        "filter[mobile]": { type: string, in: query, description: "Exact match on the stored value: E.164 for valid numbers, e.g. +492211234567." }
        "filter[mobile_work]": { type: string, in: query, description: "Exact match on the stored value: E.164 for valid numbers, e.g. +492211234567." }
        "filter[speeddial]": { type: integer, in: query, description: "Speed dial number." }
        "filter[blocked]": { type: boolean, in: query, description: "Filter on the blocked flag (true = blocklisted contacts)." }
        "filter[updated_at_gte]": *p-updated-gte
        "filter[updated_at_lte]": *p-updated-lte
        page: *p-page
        per_page: *p-per-page

    get_contact:
      method: GET
      path: /contacts/{id}
      access: read
      description: "One contact by ID (same fields as list_contacts)."
      params:
        id: { type: integer, in: path, required: true, description: "Contact ID." }
      pagination: none

    create_contact:
      method: POST
      path: /contacts
      access: write
      description: >
        Create a phone book contact. All fields are optional. Valid German
        numbers are stored in E.164 (+49...) whatever format is sent. Set
        blocked=true to block calls from the contact's numbers. Returns the
        Contact. Not retried automatically.
      params:
        first_name: { type: string, in: body }
        last_name: { type: string, in: body }
        company: { type: string, in: body }
        email: { type: string, in: body }
        email_work: { type: string, in: body }
        phone: { type: string, in: body, description: "Private landline number." }
        phone_work: { type: string, in: body, description: "Business landline number." }
        mobile: { type: string, in: body }
        mobile_work: { type: string, in: body }
        fax: { type: string, in: body }
        fax_work: { type: string, in: body }
        address: { type: string, in: body }
        address_work: { type: string, in: body }
        speeddial: { type: string, in: body, description: "Speed dial number." }
        facebook_url: { type: string, in: body }
        linkedin_url: { type: string, in: body }
        xing_url: { type: string, in: body }
        twitter_account: { type: string, in: body }
        color: { type: string, in: body, description: "Display color, e.g. #d8d9da." }
        tags: { type: array, in: body, description: "List of tag strings." }
        user_id: { type: integer, in: body, description: "User the contact belongs to." }
        blocked: { type: boolean, in: body, description: "Block calls from this contact." }
      pagination: none

    update_contact:
      method: PUT
      path: /contacts/{id}
      access: write
      description: >
        Update a contact. Only the fields sent are changed; an empty string
        clears a field; tags replaces the whole tag list. Returns the
        Contact.
      params:
        id: { type: integer, in: path, required: true, description: "Contact ID." }
        first_name: { type: string, in: body }
        last_name: { type: string, in: body }
        company: { type: string, in: body }
        email: { type: string, in: body }
        email_work: { type: string, in: body }
        phone: { type: string, in: body }
        phone_work: { type: string, in: body }
        mobile: { type: string, in: body }
        mobile_work: { type: string, in: body }
        fax: { type: string, in: body }
        fax_work: { type: string, in: body }
        address: { type: string, in: body }
        address_work: { type: string, in: body }
        speeddial: { type: string, in: body }
        facebook_url: { type: string, in: body }
        linkedin_url: { type: string, in: body }
        xing_url: { type: string, in: body }
        twitter_account: { type: string, in: body }
        color: { type: string, in: body }
        tags: { type: array, in: body, description: "Complete new list of tag strings." }
        user_id: { type: integer, in: body }
        blocked: { type: boolean, in: body }
      pagination: none

    delete_contact:
      method: DELETE
      path: /contacts/{id}
      access: dangerous
      description: "Delete a contact. Irreversible. Returns no body (204)."
      params:
        id: { type: integer, in: path, required: true, description: "Contact ID." }
      pagination: none

    # ── SMS ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    send_sms:
      method: POST
      path: /sms
      access: write
      description: >
        Send a text message (SMS) to a mobile number; SMS are billed by
        Placetel. Returns no body on success (201). Not retried automatically, so a
        timeout never causes a duplicate SMS.
      params:
        recipient: { type: string, in: body, required: true, description: "Mobile number, e.g. 01701234567 or +491701234567." }
        message: { type: string, in: body, required: true, description: "Message text." }
      pagination: none

    # ── Faxes ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    list_faxes:
      method: GET
      path: /faxes
      access: read
      description: >
        Inbound and outbound faxes, newest first: {id, type (inbound |
        outbound), from_number, to_number, pages, retries, status (queued |
        working | success | failed | busy | conversion_error), status_info
        (outbound only, e.g. a T.38 error), email, header, duration, file
        (URL of the PDF), report (URL of the transmission report PDF),
        created_at}. Paged: plain array.
      params:
        "filter[type]": { type: string, in: query, description: "inbound, outbound or 'inbound,outbound' (API default: both)." }
        "filter[from_number]": { type: string, in: query }
        "filter[to_number]": { type: string, in: query }
        order: *p-order
        page: *p-page
        per_page: *p-per-page

    get_fax:
      method: GET
      path: /faxes/{id}
      access: read
      description: "One fax by ID, e.g. to poll the status of an outbound fax (queued -> working -> success or failed/busy/conversion_error)."
      params:
        id: { type: integer, in: path, required: true, description: "Fax ID." }
      pagination: none

    send_fax:
      method: POST
      path: /faxes
      access: write
      description: >
        Send a PDF as fax. file must be a base64 data URI
        ("data:application/pdf;base64,..."); in ToolMesh pass
        "tm-blob://<id>#dataurl" after upload_file instead of inline base64.
        Returns the Fax (status queued); poll get_fax for the result. A
        status mail goes to email. Not retried automatically.
      params:
        from_number: { type: string, in: body, required: true, description: "Your fax-capable Placetel number." }
        to_number: { type: string, in: body, required: true, description: "Recipient fax number." }
        email: { type: string, in: body, required: true, description: "Address for the send report." }
        file: { type: string, in: body, required: true, description: "PDF as base64 data URI or tm-blob://<id>#dataurl." }
        header: { type: string, in: body, description: "Fax header line." }
      pagination: none

    delete_fax:
      method: DELETE
      path: /faxes/{id}
      access: dangerous
      description: "Delete a fax and its documents. Irreversible. Returns no body (204)."
      params:
        id: { type: integer, in: path, required: true, description: "Fax ID." }
      pagination: none

    # ── Numbers and number profiles ────────────────────────────────────────

    list_numbers:
      method: GET
      path: /numbers
      access: read
      description: >
        Phone numbers of the account: {id, routing_id (routing object, see
        get_routing), site_id, prefix (area code), numonly, number (national
        format), e164, activated, test_number, name, description, carrier,
        created_at, updated_at}. Paged: plain array.
      params:
        "filter[number]": { type: string, in: query, description: "Phone number in national format exactly as in number (e.g. 02211234567); E.164 and numonly find nothing." }
        "filter[prefix]": { type: string, in: query, description: "Area code, e.g. 0221." }
        "filter[name]": { type: string, in: query }
        "filter[description]": { type: string, in: query }
        "filter[site_id]": { type: integer, in: query, description: "Site (location) ID from list_sites." }
        "filter[activated]": { type: boolean, in: query, description: "Only activated (true) or inactive (false) numbers; relevant for PROFI accounts." }
        page: *p-page
        per_page: *p-per-page

    get_number:
      method: GET
      path: /numbers/{id}
      access: read
      description: "One phone number by ID (same fields as list_numbers). Follow routing_id with get_routing to see how its calls are handled."
      params:
        id: { type: integer, in: path, required: true, description: "Number ID." }
      pagination: none

    activate_number:
      method: POST
      path: /numbers/{id}/activation
      access: admin
      description: "Activate a number of the account so it takes calls. Activation may be charged. Returns the Number. Not retried automatically."
      params:
        id: { type: integer, in: path, required: true, description: "Number ID." }
      pagination: none

    deactivate_number:
      method: DELETE
      path: /numbers/{id}/activation
      access: dangerous
      description: "Deactivate a number: it stops taking calls. Returns no body (204)."
      params:
        id: { type: integer, in: path, required: true, description: "Number ID." }
      pagination: none

    list_number_profiles:
      method: GET
      path: /numbers/{number_id}/profiles
      access: read
      description: >
        Profiles of a number: saved alternative configurations (e.g. office
        hours vs. holidays), exactly one active. Each {id, name, number_id,
        active}. Switch with activate_number_profile. Empty while a number
        has only its routing; once a profile was created, the number's own
        routing object shows up as active profile "Standard" (its id equals
        Number.routing_id).
      params:
        number_id: { type: integer, in: path, required: true, description: "Number ID." }
      pagination: none

    create_number_profile:
      method: POST
      path: /numbers/{number_id}/profiles
      access: write
      description: "Create a new, inactive profile for a number. On a number without profiles Placetel also turns the number's routing object into the active profile 'Standard' and sets that routing's name to 'Standard'; deleting the new profile later does not undo this. Returns the Profile {id, name, number_id, active}. Not retried automatically."
      params:
        number_id: { type: integer, in: path, required: true, description: "Number ID." }
        name: { type: string, in: body, required: true, description: "Profile name." }
      pagination: none

    activate_number_profile:
      method: PUT
      path: /numbers/{number_id}/profiles
      access: write
      description: "Make a profile the active one for a number, which changes how the number handles calls. Returns the Profile."
      params:
        number_id: { type: integer, in: path, required: true, description: "Number ID." }
        id: { type: integer, in: body, required: true, description: "Profile ID from list_number_profiles." }
      pagination: none

    delete_number_profile:
      method: DELETE
      path: /numbers/{number_id}/profiles/{id}
      access: dangerous
      description: "Delete a profile of a number. Never delete the active profile 'Standard': its id is the number's routing object (Number.routing_id). Irreversible. Returns no body (204)."
      params:
        number_id: { type: integer, in: path, required: true, description: "Number ID." }
        id: { type: integer, in: path, required: true, description: "Profile ID." }
      pagination: none

    # ── Routings (how a number handles incoming calls) ─────────────────────

    list_routings:
      method: GET
      path: /routings
      access: read
      description: >
        Routing objects: {id, name, one behavior object (forward, group,
        plan, ivr, queue, api or ai), mailbox, notification, time_settings
        (only {enabled} while disabled), custom_caller_id ({enabled: 0 or 1,
        name, number}), music_on_hold, notify_external_api, priority,
        created_at, updated_at}. name may be null. Paged: plain array.
      params:
        "filter[updated_at_gte]": *p-updated-gte
        "filter[updated_at_lte]": *p-updated-lte
        page: *p-page
        per_page: *p-per-page

    get_routing:
      method: GET
      path: /routings/{number_or_id}
      access: read
      description: >
        The routing object of a phone number, or a routing object by ID
        (same fields as list_routings). Answers "where do calls to this
        number go?".
      params:
        number_or_id: { type: string, in: path, required: true, description: "Phone number in national format as in Number.number (e.g. 02211234567; the E.164 form answers 404) or routing object ID." }
      pagination: none

    create_routing:
      method: POST
      path: /routings
      access: write
      description: >
        Create a routing object. Set exactly ONE behavior: forward, group,
        ivr, queue or api (plan only exists on update_routing). Optional
        extras: mailbox, notification, time_settings, custom_callerid,
        music_on_hold. Standalone routing objects serve as IVR menu items,
        routing plan entries or backup targets; to change what a number does,
        call update_routing with the number instead. Defaults when omitted:
        mailbox active, notification type all with receiver global, priority
        99, time_settings disabled. Returns the RoutingObject. Not retried
        automatically.
      params:
        name: { type: string, in: body, required: true, description: "Name of the routing object." }
        forward: *p-routing-forward
        group: *p-routing-group
        ivr: *p-routing-ivr
        queue: *p-routing-queue
        api: *p-routing-api
        mailbox: *p-routing-mailbox
        notification: *p-routing-notification
        time_settings: *p-routing-time-settings
        custom_callerid: *p-routing-callerid
        music_on_hold: *p-routing-moh
        notify_external_api: *p-routing-notify-api
      pagination: none

    update_routing:
      method: PUT
      path: /routings/{number_or_id}
      access: write
      description: >
        Change how a number (or routing object) handles calls. Set ONE
        behavior: forward, group, plan, ivr, queue or api. Example: forward a
        number to a mobile phone after 20 s on the office phone with
        forward={destinations: [{targets: ['7771234567@fpbx.de'],
        ringing_time: 20}, {targets: ['+491701234567'], ringing_time: 30}],
        behaviour: 'mailbox'}. Only the objects sent change; omitted name,
        forward, time_settings or mailbox stay as they are (verified). A
        ringing_time outside the listed values is rejected with 400. Returns
        the RoutingObject.
      params:
        number_or_id: { type: string, in: path, required: true, description: "Phone number in national format (e.g. 02211234567, not E.164) or routing object ID." }
        name: { type: string, in: body, description: "Name of the routing object." }
        forward: *p-routing-forward
        group: *p-routing-group
        plan:
          type: object
          in: body
          description: "Routing plan behavior: {id: routing plan ID (required), destinations: [{targets: [...], ringing_time}]}."
        ivr: *p-routing-ivr
        queue: *p-routing-queue
        api: *p-routing-api
        mailbox: *p-routing-mailbox
        notification: *p-routing-notification
        time_settings: *p-routing-time-settings
        custom_callerid: *p-routing-callerid
        music_on_hold: *p-routing-moh
        notify_external_api: *p-routing-notify-api
      pagination: none

    delete_routing:
      method: DELETE
      path: /routings/{number_or_id}
      access: dangerous
      description: "Delete a routing object (by ID or by the number it belongs to). Calls to an affected number lose their routing. Irreversible. Returns no body (204)."
      params:
        number_or_id: { type: string, in: path, required: true, description: "Phone number in national format (e.g. 02211234567, not E.164) or routing object ID." }
      pagination: none

    # ── Routing plans ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    list_routing_plans:
      method: GET
      path: /routing_plans
      access: read
      description: >
        Routing plans: ordered sets of routing objects, each with its own
        time settings; the first active one answers. Each {id, name,
        description, did (internal extension of the plan),
        routing_object_counts, rings_for (numbers that use the plan, national
        format), created_at, updated_at}. Paged: plain array.
      params:
        page: *p-page
        per_page: *p-per-page

    get_routing_plan:
      method: GET
      path: /routing_plans/{id}
      access: read
      description: "One routing plan by ID. Its routing objects come from list_routing_plan_objects."
      params:
        id: { type: integer, in: path, required: true, description: "Routing plan ID." }
      pagination: none

    list_routing_plan_objects:
      method: GET
      path: /routing_plans/{id}/routings
      access: read
      description: "The routing objects of a routing plan, in priority order (same fields as list_routings)."
      params:
        id: { type: integer, in: path, required: true, description: "Routing plan ID." }
      pagination: none

    simulate_routing_plan:
      method: GET
      path: /routing_plans/{id}/simulate
      access: read
      description: "Which routing object of a plan would answer a call at a given time (checks time settings and holidays). Returns that RoutingObject (same fields as list_routings), or an empty result when no routing object of the plan is active at that time. Read-only."
      params:
        id: { type: integer, in: path, required: true, description: "Routing plan ID." }
        time: { type: string, in: query, description: "ISO 8601 date-time of the simulated call. Defaults to now." }
      pagination: none

    create_routing_plan:
      method: POST
      path: /routing_plans
      access: write
      description: "Create a routing plan from existing routing objects. The routing objects then belong to the plan: delete_routing_plan deletes them too. did stays null when omitted. Returns the RoutingPlan. Not retried automatically."
      params:
        name: { type: string, in: body, description: "Plan name." }
        description: { type: string, in: body }
        did: { type: string, in: body, description: "Internal extension of the plan." }
        routing_objects: { type: array, in: body, description: "Routing objects in priority order: [{id: routing object ID}]." }
      pagination: none

    update_routing_plan:
      method: PUT
      path: /routing_plans/{id}
      access: write
      description: "Update a routing plan. Without routing_objects the plan keeps its objects (verified); when sent, send the complete list in the wanted order. Returns the RoutingPlan."
      params:
        id: { type: integer, in: path, required: true, description: "Routing plan ID." }
        name: { type: string, in: body, required: true, description: "Plan name (required by the API on update)." }
        description: { type: string, in: body }
        did: { type: string, in: body, description: "Internal extension of the plan." }
        routing_objects: { type: array, in: body, description: "[{id: routing object ID, priority: integer}]." }
      pagination: none

    delete_routing_plan:
      method: DELETE
      path: /routing_plans/{id}
      access: dangerous
      description: "Delete a routing plan AND the routing objects in it (verified: a routing object of the plan was gone afterwards). Check list_routing_plan_objects, SIP users (routing_plan_id) and routings with plan behavior first. Irreversible. Returns no body (204)."
      params:
        id: { type: integer, in: path, required: true, description: "Routing plan ID." }
      pagination: none

    # ── SIP users (extensions) and short codes ─────────────────────────────

    list_sip_users:
      method: GET
      path: /sip_users
      access: read
      description: >
        SIP users (phone extensions): {id, sipuid, username, domain, name,
        description, did (internal extension), callerid (outbound caller
        ID), type (standard | blf | fax | trunk | legacy_standard),
        webuser_id and webuser (owning user), automatic_prefix,
        blocked_prefixes, routing_plan_id (fallback when busy or
        unanswered), online, registrations (active SIP registrations with
        user_agent, received address, expires, ...), busy_on_busy,
        contact_speeddialing, p_asserted_identity, hotdesk_login,
        hotdesk_type, cost_center, created_at, updated_at}. hotdesk_pin is
        masked ([REDACTED]); password only appears in get_sip_user and
        create_sip_user, masked as well. Paged: plain array.
      params:
        "filter[did]": { type: integer, in: query, description: "Internal extension number." }
        "filter[username]": { type: string, in: query, description: "SIP username (the part before @ of the sipuid)." }
        "filter[name]": { type: string, in: query }
        "filter[description]": { type: string, in: query }
        page: *p-page
        per_page: *p-per-page
      response:
        result_path: "$"
        redact: *redact-sip-user-list

    get_sip_user:
      method: GET
      path: /sip_users/{id}
      access: read
      description: "One SIP user by ID (same fields as list_sip_users; online shows the current registration state). The SIP password and hotdesk PIN are masked."
      params:
        id: { type: integer, in: path, required: true, description: "SIP user ID." }
      response:
        result_path: "$"
        redact: *redact-sip-user
      pagination: none

    create_sip_user:
      method: POST
      path: /sip_users
      access: write
      description: >
        Create a SIP user (phone extension). Returns the SipUser; the
        generated SIP password is masked here, read it in the web portal.
        Not retried automatically.
      params:
        name: { type: string, in: body, required: true }
        type: { type: string, in: body, required: true, description: "standard, blf, fax, trunk or legacy_standard." }
        description: { type: string, in: body }
        did: { type: integer, in: body, description: "Internal extension number." }
        callerid: { type: string, in: body, description: "Outbound caller ID (one of the account's numbers)." }
        webuser_id: { type: integer, in: body, description: "Owning user ID (list_users)." }
        contact_speeddialing: { type: boolean, in: body }
        automatic_prefix: { type: string, in: body, description: "Prefix prepended to outbound calls, e.g. an area code 0221." }
        blocked_prefixes: { type: string, in: body, description: "Comma-separated list of blocked destination prefixes." }
        busy_on_busy: { type: boolean, in: body, description: "Signal busy to further callers while on a call." }
        routing_plan_id: { type: integer, in: body, description: "Fallback routing plan when busy or unanswered." }
        hotdesk_login: { type: string, in: body }
        hotdesk_pin: { type: string, in: body }
        hotdesk_type: { type: string, in: body, description: "standard, custom or global_did." }
        hotdesk_provisioning_id: { type: integer, in: body, description: "Provisioned phone used for hotdesking." }
      response:
        result_path: "$"
        redact: *redact-sip-user
      pagination: none

    update_sip_user:
      method: PUT
      path: /sip_users/{id}
      access: write
      description: >
        Update a SIP user; send the fields to change (the type cannot be
        changed). Returns the SipUser with masked secrets.
      params:
        id: { type: integer, in: path, required: true, description: "SIP user ID." }
        name: { type: string, in: body }
        description: { type: string, in: body }
        did: { type: integer, in: body, description: "Internal extension number." }
        callerid: { type: string, in: body, description: "Outbound caller ID." }
        p_asserted_identity: { type: string, in: body, description: "P-Asserted-Identity number for outbound calls." }
        webuser_id: { type: integer, in: body }
        contact_speeddialing: { type: boolean, in: body }
        automatic_prefix: { type: string, in: body }
        blocked_prefixes: { type: string, in: body, description: "Comma-separated list of blocked destination prefixes." }
        busy_on_busy: { type: boolean, in: body }
        routing_plan_id: { type: integer, in: body }
        hotdesk_login: { type: string, in: body }
        hotdesk_pin: { type: string, in: body }
        hotdesk_type: { type: string, in: body, description: "standard, custom or global_did." }
        hotdesk_provisioning_id: { type: integer, in: body }
      response:
        result_path: "$"
        redact: *redact-sip-user
      pagination: none

    delete_sip_user:
      method: DELETE
      path: /sip_users/{id}
      access: dangerous
      description: "Delete a SIP user; phones registered with it stop working. Irreversible. Returns no body (204)."
      params:
        id: { type: integer, in: path, required: true, description: "SIP user ID." }
      pagination: none

    list_sip_user_short_codes:
      method: GET
      path: /sip_users/{id}/short_codes
      access: read
      description: "Short codes (star codes dialed on the phone) of a SIP user: {id, code, action, number, group_id, description, created_at, updated_at}."
      params:
        id: { type: integer, in: path, required: true, description: "SIP user ID." }
      pagination: none

    create_sip_user_short_code:
      method: POST
      path: /sip_users/{id}/short_codes
      access: write
      description: >
        Create a short code for a SIP user. action: set_out_anonymous,
        set_forward, clear_forward, login_group (needs group_id), mailbox,
        profile, set_out_number (needs number), addto_routing. code must be
        one of Placetel's predefined codes: a free code such as *987 is
        rejected with 400 "Validation failed: Code is not included in the
        list". The API reference does not list the allowed codes; the
        short code dialog of the web portal shows them. Returns the
        ShortCode. Not retried automatically.
      params:
        id: { type: integer, in: path, required: true, description: "SIP user ID." }
        code: { type: string, in: body, required: true, description: "Digits to dial." }
        action: { type: string, in: body, required: true, description: "One of the actions listed above." }
        number: { type: string, in: body, description: "Number for actions that need one (e.g. set_forward, set_out_number)." }
        group_id: { type: integer, in: body, description: "Group for login_group." }
        description: { type: string, in: body }
      pagination: none

    delete_sip_user_short_code:
      method: DELETE
      path: /sip_users/{id}/short_codes/{code_id}
      access: dangerous
      description: "Delete a short code of a SIP user. Returns no body (204)."
      params:
        id: { type: integer, in: path, required: true, description: "SIP user ID." }
        code_id: { type: integer, in: path, required: true, description: "Short code ID." }
      pagination: none

    # ── Groups (ring groups) ───────────────────────────────────────────────

    list_groups:
      method: GET
      path: /groups
      access: read
      description: >
        Groups of SIP users: {id, name, description, type (ring_all | hunt |
        monitoring), members (SipUser objects, secrets masked), created_at,
        updated_at}. Paged: plain array.
      params:
        "filter[name]": { type: string, in: query }
        "filter[description]": { type: string, in: query }
        "filter[type]": { type: string, in: query, description: "ring_all, hunt or monitoring." }
        page: *p-page
        per_page: *p-per-page
      response:
        result_path: "$"
        redact: *redact-group-list

    get_group:
      method: GET
      path: /groups/{id}
      access: read
      description: "One group by ID with its members."
      params:
        id: { type: integer, in: path, required: true, description: "Group ID." }
      response:
        result_path: "$"
        redact: *redact-group
      pagination: none

    create_group:
      method: POST
      path: /groups
      access: write
      description: "Create a group of SIP users. Use it as a routing target (group behavior). Returns the Group. Not retried automatically."
      params:
        name: { type: string, in: body, required: true }
        type: { type: string, in: body, required: true, description: "ring_all (all members ring at once), hunt or monitoring." }
        description: { type: string, in: body }
        member_ids: { type: array, in: body, description: "SIP user IDs (integers)." }
      response:
        result_path: "$"
        redact: *redact-group
      pagination: none

    update_group:
      method: PUT
      path: /groups/{id}
      access: write
      description: "Update a group (the type cannot be changed). member_ids replaces the whole member list; omit it to keep the members (both verified). Returns the Group."
      params:
        id: { type: integer, in: path, required: true, description: "Group ID." }
        name: { type: string, in: body }
        description: { type: string, in: body }
        member_ids: { type: array, in: body, description: "Complete list of member SIP user IDs." }
      response:
        result_path: "$"
        redact: *redact-group
      pagination: none

    delete_group:
      method: DELETE
      path: /groups/{id}
      access: dangerous
      description: "Delete a group. Check routings that ring it (group behavior) first. Irreversible. Returns no body (204)."
      params:
        id: { type: integer, in: path, required: true, description: "Group ID." }
      pagination: none

    # ── Prompts (announcements) ────────────────────────────────────────────

    list_prompts:
      method: GET
      path: /prompts
      access: read
      description: "Announcements used by IVRs, queues, mailboxes and forwards: {id, name, description, text, file (signed URL of the audio, valid for about 5 minutes; fetch a fresh one with get_prompt), created_at, updated_at}. filter[name] is an exact match. Paged: plain array."
      params:
        "filter[name]": { type: string, in: query }
        "filter[description]": { type: string, in: query }
        page: *p-page
        per_page: *p-per-page

    get_prompt:
      method: GET
      path: /prompts/{id}
      access: read
      description: "One prompt by ID. file is a freshly signed audio URL, valid for about 5 minutes: download right away."
      params:
        id: { type: integer, in: path, required: true, description: "Prompt ID." }
      pagination: none

    create_prompt:
      method: POST
      path: /prompts
      access: write
      description: >
        Create an announcement, either synthesized from text with a voice or
        from an uploaded audio file (base64 data URI; in ToolMesh
        tm-blob://<id>#dataurl). voice is required by the API in both cases
        but not returned. Synthesis runs asynchronously: the file URL in this
        response can answer 404 for a few seconds; call get_prompt shortly
        after for the final audio (synthesized text came back as WAV, 8 kHz
        mono, telephone quality). Returns the Prompt. Not retried
        automatically.
      params:
        name: { type: string, in: body, required: true }
        voice:
          type: string
          in: body
          required: true
          description: "Text-to-speech voice. Language-prefixed voices: de-DE-Wavenet-G, de-DE-Wavenet-H, de-DE-Chirp3-HD-Erinome, de-DE-Chirp3-HD-Enceladus, de-DE-Chirp3-HD-Sadachbia, de-DE-Chirp3-HD-Sulafat, en-GB-Neural2-A/B/C/D/F, en-GB-Standard-A/B, en-US-Neural2-A/C/D/E/F/G/H/I/J, en-US-Wavenet-A/C/F, es-ES-Neural2-A/B/C/D/E/F, es-ES-Standard-A, fr-FR-Neural2-A/B/C/D/E, fr-FR-Wavenet-A/B, it-IT-Neural2-A/C, it-IT-Wavenet-A/C, ja-JP-Wavenet-A, ko-KR-Standard-A, nl-NL-Wavenet-A/C/D, pt-BR-Standard-A, pt-PT-Wavenet-A/B, sv-SE-Standard-A, sv-SE-Wavenet-A/C, tr-TR-Standard-A, tr-TR-Wavenet-A/B (write the full name, e.g. en-GB-Neural2-A). The API also accepts a set of 20-character voice IDs listed in its reference."
        text: { type: string, in: body, description: "Text to synthesize." }
        file: { type: string, in: body, description: "Audio file as base64 data URI or tm-blob://<id>#dataurl (instead of text)." }
        description: { type: string, in: body }
      pagination: none

    update_prompt:
      method: PUT
      path: /prompts/{id}
      access: write
      description: "Update a prompt (new text, voice or audio file). name and voice are required by the API. A new text is synthesized again, asynchronously, and gets a new file URL (see create_prompt). Returns the Prompt."
      params:
        id: { type: integer, in: path, required: true, description: "Prompt ID." }
        name: { type: string, in: body, required: true }
        voice: { type: string, in: body, required: true, description: "Text-to-speech voice, see create_prompt." }
        text: { type: string, in: body }
        file: { type: string, in: body, description: "Audio file as base64 data URI or tm-blob://<id>#dataurl." }
        description: { type: string, in: body }
      pagination: none

    delete_prompt:
      method: DELETE
      path: /prompts/{id}
      access: dangerous
      description: "Delete a prompt. Check IVRs, queues, forwards and mailboxes that play it first. Irreversible. Returns no body (204)."
      params:
        id: { type: integer, in: path, required: true, description: "Prompt ID." }
      pagination: none

    # ── Call center (agents, queues, queue calls) ──────────────────────────

    list_call_center_agents:
      method: GET
      path: /call_center_agents
      access: read
      description: >
        Call center agents: {id, name, description, extension_type (SIP |
        PSTN), extension_sip, extension_pstn, agent_type (Agent |
        Supervisor), status (offline | online | dail_out | working | pause),
        priority, last_call_at, created_at, updated_at}. Needs the call
        center product; without it the API answers 404. Paged: plain array.
      params:
        page: *p-page
        per_page: *p-per-page

    create_call_center_agent:
      method: POST
      path: /call_center_agents
      access: write
      description: >
        Create a call center agent that is reached either on a SIP extension
        or on an external (PSTN) number, chosen by extension_type. The API
        requires both extension fields. Returns the CallCenterAgent. Not
        retried automatically.
      params:
        name: { type: string, in: body, required: true }
        extension_type: { type: string, in: body, required: true, description: "SIP or PSTN." }
        extension_sip: { type: string, in: body, required: true, description: "sipuid of the agent, e.g. 7771234567@fpbx.de." }
        extension_pstn: { type: string, in: body, required: true, description: "External number of the agent, e.g. +492211234567." }
        agent_type: { type: string, in: body, description: "Agent (default) or Supervisor." }
        description: { type: string, in: body }
        priority: { type: integer, in: body, description: "Agent priority in the queues." }
      pagination: none

    update_call_center_agent:
      method: PUT
      path: /call_center_agents/{id}
      access: write
      description: >
        Update an agent, e.g. set status to online, pause or offline. The
        API requires extension_sip and extension_pstn on every update: send
        the current values from list_call_center_agents. Returns the
        CallCenterAgent.
      params:
        id: { type: integer, in: path, required: true, description: "Agent ID." }
        extension_sip: { type: string, in: body, required: true, description: "Current or new sipuid of the agent." }
        extension_pstn: { type: string, in: body, required: true, description: "Current or new external number of the agent." }
        extension_type: { type: string, in: body, description: "SIP or PSTN." }
        status: { type: string, in: body, description: "offline, online, dail_out, working or pause (API spelling)." }
        name: { type: string, in: body }
        description: { type: string, in: body }
        priority: { type: integer, in: body }
      pagination: none

    list_call_center_queues:
      method: GET
      path: /call_center_queues
      access: read
      description: >
        Call center queues: {id, name, description, num_loops, priority,
        ringing_time, max_iterations, mail_notification, play_prompt and
        prompt (greeting), play_prompt_waiting and prompt_waiting,
        play_prompt_end and prompt_end, play_mailbox and prompt_mailbox,
        created_at, updated_at}. Paged: plain array.
      params:
        page: *p-page
        per_page: *p-per-page

    create_call_center_queue:
      method: POST
      path: /call_center_queues
      access: write
      description: "Create a call center queue; route a number to it with update_routing (queue behavior). Returns the CallCenterQueue. Not retried automatically."
      params:
        name: { type: string, in: body, required: true, description: "Queue name." }
        description: { type: string, in: body }
        priority: { type: integer, in: body, description: "Queue priority (API default 0)." }
        num_loops: { type: integer, in: body, description: "API default 3." }
        ringing_time: { type: integer, in: body, description: "Seconds an agent rings (API default 30)." }
        max_iterations: { type: integer, in: body, description: "API default 10." }
        mail_notification: { type: string, in: body, description: "E-mail address for notifications." }
        play_prompt: { type: boolean, in: body, description: "Play a greeting (prompt_id)." }
        prompt_id: { type: integer, in: body }
        play_prompt_waiting: { type: boolean, in: body, description: "Play a waiting announcement (prompt_waiting_id)." }
        prompt_waiting_id: { type: integer, in: body }
        play_prompt_end: { type: boolean, in: body, description: "Play an end announcement (prompt_end_id)." }
        prompt_end_id: { type: integer, in: body }
        play_mailbox: { type: boolean, in: body, description: "Offer the mailbox (prompt_mailbox_id)." }
        prompt_mailbox_id: { type: integer, in: body }
      pagination: none

    update_call_center_queue:
      method: PUT
      path: /call_center_queues/{id}
      access: write
      description: "Update a call center queue; send the fields to change. Returns the CallCenterQueue."
      params:
        id: { type: integer, in: path, required: true, description: "Queue ID." }
        name: { type: string, in: body }
        description: { type: string, in: body }
        priority: { type: integer, in: body }
        num_loops: { type: integer, in: body }
        ringing_time: { type: integer, in: body, description: "Seconds an agent rings." }
        max_iterations: { type: integer, in: body }
        mail_notification: { type: string, in: body }
        play_prompt: { type: boolean, in: body }
        prompt_id: { type: integer, in: body }
        play_prompt_waiting: { type: boolean, in: body }
        prompt_waiting_id: { type: integer, in: body }
        play_prompt_end: { type: boolean, in: body }
        prompt_end_id: { type: integer, in: body }
        play_mailbox: { type: boolean, in: body }
        prompt_mailbox_id: { type: integer, in: body }
      pagination: none

    list_call_center_calls:
      method: GET
      path: /call_center_calls
      access: read
      description: >
        Queue calls of ONE day: {id, call_type (dail_in | dail_out),
        call_status (unassigned | assigned | ended | not_answered |
        cancelled | dail_out), answer_status, started_at, left_queue_at,
        ended_at, last_updated_at, iteration, from, to, queue_name,
        agent_name}. unassigned calls are waiting and can be picked with
        pick_call_center_call. Needs the call center product (404
        otherwise). Paged: plain array.
      params:
        date: { type: string, in: query, required: true, description: "Day as YYYY-MM-DD." }
        "queue_ids[]": { type: integer, in: query, description: "Only calls of this ONE queue (array filter, one value per call)." }
        page: *p-page
        per_page: *p-per-page

    pick_call_center_call:
      method: POST
      path: /call_center_calls/{id}/pick
      access: write
      description: "Hand a waiting queue call to a given agent. Returns the CallCenterCall. Not retried automatically."
      params:
        id: { type: integer, in: path, required: true, description: "Call center call ID." }
        sipuid: { type: string, in: body, required: true, description: "sipuid of the agent who takes the call." }
      pagination: none

    # ── CTI call control (desk phones provisioned through Placetel) ────────

    dial_cti_number:
      method: POST
      path: /cti/{mac}/dial
      access: write
      description: "Start a new call from a provisioned desk phone. Not retried automatically. Returns no body (201)."
      params:
        mac: { type: string, in: path, required: true, description: "MAC address of the phone (mac from list_provisionings)." }
        line: { type: integer, in: body, required: true, description: "Line (account) on the phone." }
        number: { type: string, in: body, required: true, description: "Number or extension to dial." }
      pagination: none

    answer_cti_call:
      method: POST
      path: /cti/{mac}/answer
      access: write
      description: "Answer a ringing call on a provisioned desk phone. Returns no body (201)."
      params:
        mac: { type: string, in: path, required: true, description: "MAC address of the phone." }
        line: { type: integer, in: body, required: true, description: "Line on the phone." }
        call_id: { type: integer, in: body, required: true, description: "Phone-side call ID (integer)." }
      pagination: none

    decline_cti_call:
      method: POST
      path: /cti/{mac}/decline
      access: write
      description: "Decline a ringing call on a provisioned desk phone. Returns no body (201)."
      params:
        mac: { type: string, in: path, required: true, description: "MAC address of the phone." }
        line: { type: integer, in: body, required: true }
        call_id: { type: integer, in: body, required: true, description: "Phone-side call ID." }
      pagination: none

    hangup_cti_call:
      method: POST
      path: /cti/{mac}/hangup
      access: write
      description: "End a call on a provisioned desk phone. Returns no body (201)."
      params:
        mac: { type: string, in: path, required: true, description: "MAC address of the phone." }
        line: { type: integer, in: body, required: true }
        call_id: { type: integer, in: body, required: true, description: "Phone-side call ID." }
      pagination: none

    hold_cti_call:
      method: POST
      path: /cti/{mac}/hold
      access: write
      description: "Put a call on hold on a provisioned desk phone. Returns no body (201)."
      params:
        mac: { type: string, in: path, required: true, description: "MAC address of the phone." }
        line: { type: integer, in: body, required: true }
        call_id: { type: integer, in: body, required: true, description: "Phone-side call ID." }
      pagination: none

    resume_cti_call:
      method: POST
      path: /cti/{mac}/resume
      access: write
      description: "Resume a held call on a provisioned desk phone. Returns no body (201)."
      params:
        mac: { type: string, in: path, required: true, description: "MAC address of the phone." }
        line: { type: integer, in: body, required: true }
        call_id: { type: integer, in: body, required: true, description: "Phone-side call ID." }
      pagination: none

    transfer_cti_call:
      method: POST
      path: /cti/{mac}/blind_transfer
      access: write
      description: "Blind transfer: hand a call on a provisioned desk phone to another number without consultation. Returns no body (201)."
      params:
        mac: { type: string, in: path, required: true, description: "MAC address of the phone." }
        line: { type: integer, in: body, required: true }
        call_id: { type: integer, in: body, required: true, description: "Phone-side call ID." }
        number: { type: string, in: body, required: true, description: "Transfer target number or extension." }
      pagination: none

    start_cti_transfer:
      method: POST
      path: /cti/{mac}/start_transfer
      access: write
      description: "Attended transfer, step 1: start the transfer of a call on a provisioned desk phone; finish with complete_cti_transfer. The API reference does not say how the target is chosen, so for a known target prefer transfer_cti_call. Returns no body (201)."
      params:
        mac: { type: string, in: path, required: true, description: "MAC address of the phone." }
        line: { type: integer, in: body, required: true }
        call_id: { type: integer, in: body, required: true, description: "Phone-side call ID." }
      pagination: none

    complete_cti_transfer:
      method: POST
      path: /cti/{mac}/complete_transfer
      access: write
      description: "Attended transfer, last step: connect the parties of a transfer started with start_cti_transfer. Returns no body (201)."
      params:
        mac: { type: string, in: path, required: true, description: "MAC address of the phone." }
        line: { type: integer, in: body, required: true }
        call_id: { type: integer, in: body, required: true, description: "Phone-side call ID." }
      pagination: none

    start_cti_conference:
      method: POST
      path: /cti/{mac}/start_conference
      access: write
      description: "Start a conference from a call on a provisioned desk phone. Finish with complete_cti_conference. Returns no body (201)."
      params:
        mac: { type: string, in: path, required: true, description: "MAC address of the phone." }
        line: { type: integer, in: body, required: true }
        call_id: { type: integer, in: body, required: true, description: "Phone-side call ID." }
      pagination: none

    complete_cti_conference:
      method: POST
      path: /cti/{mac}/complete_conference
      access: write
      description: "Join the parties of a conference started with start_cti_conference. Returns no body (201)."
      params:
        mac: { type: string, in: path, required: true, description: "MAC address of the phone." }
        line: { type: integer, in: body, required: true }
        call_id: { type: integer, in: body, required: true, description: "Phone-side call ID." }
      pagination: none

    dial_cti_digit:
      method: POST
      path: /cti/{mac}/dial_digit
      access: write
      description: "Send a single digit on a call of a provisioned desk phone. For tone sequences on the active call use send_cti_dtmf_digits. Returns no body (201)."
      params:
        mac: { type: string, in: path, required: true, description: "MAC address of the phone." }
        line: { type: integer, in: body, required: true }
        call_id: { type: integer, in: body, required: true, description: "Phone-side call ID." }
        digit: { type: string, in: body, required: true, description: "One digit, 0-9, * or #." }
      pagination: none

    send_cti_dtmf_digits:
      method: POST
      path: /cti/{mac}/send_dtmf_digits
      access: write
      description: "Send DTMF tones on the currently active call of a provisioned desk phone, e.g. to navigate a remote voice menu. Returns no body (201)."
      params:
        mac: { type: string, in: path, required: true, description: "MAC address of the phone." }
        digits: { type: string, in: body, required: true, description: "Digits to send, e.g. 1#." }
      pagination: none

    get_cti_config:
      method: GET
      path: /cti/{mac}
      access: read
      description: "Read a configuration parameter of a provisioned desk phone. Parameter names depend on the phone model."
      params:
        mac: { type: string, in: path, required: true, description: "MAC address of the phone." }
        "params[]": { type: string, in: query, required: true, description: "ONE parameter name per call (array parameter)." }
      pagination: none

    set_cti_config:
      method: PUT
      path: /cti/{mac}
      access: admin
      description: "Set configuration parameters on a provisioned desk phone. Wrong values can make the phone unusable."
      params:
        mac: { type: string, in: path, required: true, description: "MAC address of the phone." }
        params: { type: object, in: body, required: true, description: "Map of parameter name to value; names depend on the phone model." }
      pagination: none

    # ── Users (web portal logins, permissions) ─────────────────────────────

    list_users:
      method: GET
      path: /users
      access: read
      description: >
        Users (web portal logins) of the account: {id, login, email,
        first_name, last_name, type (main_account | subuser), did and
        callerid of the primary SIP user, primary_sip_user_id, locale,
        admin_user, rights_numbers, permissions {enabled, blocks},
        obfuscate_billing_records, obfuscate_others,
        two_factor_authentication_enabled, numbers, created_at, updated_at}.
        Paged: plain array.
      params:
        "filter[first_name]": { type: string, in: query }
        "filter[last_name]": { type: string, in: query }
        "filter[email]": { type: string, in: query }
        "filter[login]": { type: string, in: query }
        "filter[type]": { type: string, in: query, description: "main_account or subuser." }
        page: *p-page
        per_page: *p-per-page

    get_user:
      method: GET
      path: /users/{id}
      access: read
      description: "One user by ID (same fields as list_users)."
      params:
        id: { type: integer, in: path, required: true, description: "User ID." }
      pagination: none

    create_user:
      method: POST
      path: /users
      access: admin
      description: >
        Create a subuser, optionally with an extension and a phone. A
        subuser without email cannot log in to the web portal. Returns the
        User. Not retried automatically.
      params:
        first_name: { type: string, in: body, required: true }
        last_name: { type: string, in: body, required: true }
        email: { type: string, in: body, description: "Login e-mail; without it the subuser cannot use the web portal." }
        did: { type: integer, in: body, description: "Internal extension number." }
        assign_did: { type: boolean, in: body, description: "Assign a free extension automatically (API default false)." }
        callerid: { type: string, in: body, description: "Number shown on outgoing calls." }
        phone_model: { type: string, in: body, description: "Phone model name as listed by list_devices." }
        phone_mac: { type: string, in: body, description: "MAC address of the phone to provision." }
        sip_user_type: { type: string, in: body, description: "standard (default) or blf." }
      pagination: none

    update_user:
      method: PUT
      path: /users/{id}
      access: admin
      description: >
        Update a subuser: name, e-mail, extension, caller ID, admin rights,
        visible numbers, privacy and portal permissions. permissions.blocks
        lists portal areas the user may NOT open: billing_record/index,
        invoice/index, addresses/edit, order, simple/numbers, /fax,
        /sip_users, simple/index, routing_plans/index, details/robjectlist,
        simple/groups, groups/edit, provisioning/index, prompts/index,
        contacts, /cc, :cc_reporting. Returns the User.
      params:
        id: { type: integer, in: path, required: true, description: "User ID." }
        first_name: { type: string, in: body }
        last_name: { type: string, in: body }
        email: { type: string, in: body }
        did: { type: integer, in: body, description: "Internal extension number." }
        callerid: { type: string, in: body, description: "Outgoing caller ID." }
        primary_sip_user_id: { type: integer, in: body }
        admin_user: { type: boolean, in: body, description: "Grant admin rights." }
        rights_numbers: { type: array, in: body, description: "Numbers (strings) this user may see." }
        locale: { type: string, in: body, description: "de or en." }
        obfuscate_billing_records: { type: boolean, in: body, description: "Mask billing records for this user." }
        obfuscate_others: { type: boolean, in: body, description: "Mask numbers outside rights_numbers." }
        permissions: { type: object, in: body, description: "{enabled: boolean (default true), blocks: [blocked portal areas, see above]}." }
        avatar: { type: string, in: body, description: "Image as base64 data URI or tm-blob://<id>#dataurl." }
      pagination: none

    delete_user:
      method: DELETE
      path: /users/{id}
      access: dangerous
      description: "Delete a subuser. Irreversible. Returns no body (204)."
      params:
        id: { type: integer, in: path, required: true, description: "Subuser ID." }
      pagination: none

    reset_user_password:
      method: POST
      path: /users/{id}/password_reset
      access: admin
      description: "Start a password reset for a user (answers 202 without body; 400 when not possible). Not retried automatically."
      params:
        id: { type: integer, in: path, required: true, description: "User ID." }
      pagination: none

    reset_user_two_factor_authentication:
      method: DELETE
      path: /users/{id}/two_factor_authentication
      access: dangerous
      description: "Remove a user's two-factor authentication so it must be set up again. Lowers account security until then. Answers 202 without body; 400 when not possible."
      params:
        id: { type: integer, in: path, required: true, description: "User ID." }
      pagination: none

    # ── Sites (locations) ──────────────────────────────────────────────────

    list_sites:
      method: GET
      path: /sites
      access: read
      description: "Sites (locations) of the account: {id, name, street, street_no, zip, city, country, prefix (area code)}. Numbers refer to them via site_id. Paged: plain array."
      params:
        page: *p-page
        per_page: *p-per-page

    get_site:
      method: GET
      path: /sites/{id}
      access: read
      description: "One site by ID."
      params:
        id: { type: integer, in: path, required: true, description: "Site ID." }
      pagination: none

    # ── Devices and phone provisioning ─────────────────────────────────────

    list_devices:
      method: GET
      path: /devices
      access: read
      description: "Catalog of phone models Placetel can provision: {id, name, display_name, manufacturer, lines, blf_keys, expansion_keys, max_expansion_modules, dect_lines, multicell, encryptable}. Use id as phone_model in create_provisioning. Paged: plain array."
      params:
        page: *p-page
        per_page: *p-per-page

    list_provisionings:
      method: GET
      path: /provisionings
      access: read
      description: >
        Phones provisioned through Placetel: {id, name, mac, webuser,
        device (model), lines [{sipuid, position}], keys [{type, label,
        value, position}], codec, call_waiting, locale, encryption,
        custom_configurations}. The mac is the address for the CTI tools.
        Paged: plain array.
      params:
        search: { type: string, in: query, description: "Free text search, e.g. name or MAC address." }
        webuser_id: { type: integer, in: query, description: "Only phones of this user." }
        page: *p-page
        per_page: *p-per-page

    get_provisioning:
      method: GET
      path: /provisionings/{id}
      access: read
      description: "One provisioned phone by ID."
      params:
        id: { type: integer, in: path, required: true, description: "Provisioning ID." }
      pagination: none

    create_provisioning:
      method: POST
      path: /provisionings
      access: write
      description: >
        Register a phone for auto-provisioning. lines lists sipuids in line
        order; keys sets function keys [{type: blf | line | none | dtmf |
        speeddial | manual | redirect | keyevent | url, value, label}].
        Returns the Provisioning. Not retried automatically.
      params:
        name: { type: string, in: body, required: true }
        mac: { type: string, in: body, required: true, description: "MAC address of the phone." }
        phone_model: { type: integer, in: body, required: true, description: "Device ID from list_devices." }
        webuser_id: { type: integer, in: body, description: "User the phone belongs to." }
        lines: { type: array, in: body, description: "sipuids (strings) in line order." }
        keys: { type: array, in: body, description: "Function keys, see description." }
        codec: { type: string, in: body, description: "G711a, G729a, G722 or OPUS." }
        call_waiting: { type: boolean, in: body }
        encryption: { type: string, in: body, description: "disabled, enabled or template." }
        locale: { type: string, in: body, description: "de, en, fr or en-GB." }
      pagination: none

    update_provisioning:
      method: PUT
      path: /provisionings/{id}
      access: write
      description: "Update a provisioned phone (name, owner, lines, keys, codec, ...). The phone fetches changes on its next configuration update or after reconfigure_provisioning. Returns the Provisioning."
      params:
        id: { type: integer, in: path, required: true, description: "Provisioning ID." }
        name: { type: string, in: body }
        webuser_id: { type: integer, in: body }
        lines: { type: array, in: body, description: "sipuids (strings) in line order." }
        keys: { type: array, in: body, description: "Function keys [{type, value, label}], see create_provisioning." }
        codec: { type: string, in: body, description: "G711a, G729a, G722 or OPUS." }
        call_waiting: { type: boolean, in: body }
        encryption: { type: string, in: body, description: "disabled, enabled or template." }
        locale: { type: string, in: body, description: "de, en, fr or en-GB." }
      pagination: none

    delete_provisioning:
      method: DELETE
      path: /provisionings/{id}
      access: dangerous
      description: "Remove a phone from provisioning. Irreversible. Returns no body (204)."
      params:
        id: { type: integer, in: path, required: true, description: "Provisioning ID." }
      pagination: none

    reconfigure_provisioning:
      method: POST
      path: /provisionings/{id}/reconfigure
      access: write
      description: "Tell the phone to fetch its configuration now (SIP command to the user on line 1). Returns the Provisioning."
      params:
        id: { type: integer, in: path, required: true, description: "Provisioning ID." }
      pagination: none

    get_provisioning_custom_configurations:
      method: GET
      path: /provisionings/{id}/custom_configurations
      access: read
      description: "Custom configuration keys of a provisioned phone: {id, key, value, attributes}."
      params:
        id: { type: integer, in: path, required: true, description: "Provisioning ID." }
      pagination: none

    set_provisioning_custom_configuration:
      method: PUT
      path: /provisionings/{id}/custom_configurations
      access: admin
      description: "Create or update a raw configuration key of a provisioned phone (model-specific; wrong values can break the phone). Returns the Provisioning."
      params:
        id: { type: integer, in: path, required: true, description: "Provisioning ID." }
        configurations: { type: object, in: body, required: true, description: "{key (required), value (required), attributes}." }
      pagination: none

    delete_provisioning_custom_configuration:
      method: DELETE
      path: /provisionings/{id}/custom_configurations/{custom_configuration_id}
      access: dangerous
      description: "Delete a custom configuration key of a provisioned phone. Returns no body (204)."
      params:
        id: { type: integer, in: path, required: true, description: "Provisioning ID." }
        custom_configuration_id: { type: integer, in: path, required: true, description: "Custom configuration ID." }
      pagination: none

    # ── SIM cards (Placetel Mobile) ────────────────────────────────────────

    list_sim_cards:
      method: GET
      path: /sim_cards
      access: read
      description: "Mobile SIM cards: {id, card_type, iccid (after activation), contract, number, status, sip_user (secrets masked), created_at, updated_at}. Paged: plain array."
      params:
        "filter[status]": { type: string, in: query, description: "ordered, sent, in_activation, activated, port_in_progress, pending_cancellation, terminated, activation_canceled or order_canceled." }
        page: *p-page
        per_page: *p-per-page
      response:
        result_path: "$"
        redact: *redact-sim-card-list

    get_sim_card:
      method: GET
      path: /sim_cards/{id}
      access: read
      description: "One SIM card by ID."
      params:
        id: { type: integer, in: path, required: true, description: "SIM card ID." }
      response:
        result_path: "$"
        redact: *redact-sim-card
      pagination: none

    # ── Subscriptions (call event webhooks) ────────────────────────────────

    list_subscriptions:
      method: GET
      path: /subscriptions
      access: read
      description: "Registered webhook subscriptions: {id (e.g. sub-...), url, incoming, outgoing, hungup, accepted, phone, numbers}."
      pagination: none

    create_subscription:
      method: PUT
      path: /subscriptions
      access: admin
      description: >
        Register a URL that receives call events: incoming and outgoing
        calls, accepted calls, hang-ups and CTI phone events, optionally only
        for some numbers. Per Placetel's Notify API documentation events
        arrive as form-encoded POSTs (event, call_id, from, to, direction).
        Call data leaves Placetel, so only register endpoints you control. Returns the Subscription. Not retried
        automatically.
      params:
        service: { type: string, in: body, required: true, description: "Free label naming your integration." }
        url: { type: string, in: body, required: true, description: "HTTPS endpoint that receives the events." }
        incoming: { type: boolean, in: body, description: "Incoming calls (API default false)." }
        outgoing: { type: boolean, in: body, description: "Outgoing calls." }
        accepted: { type: boolean, in: body, description: "Answered calls." }
        hungup: { type: boolean, in: body, description: "Ended calls." }
        phone: { type: boolean, in: body, description: "CTI events of provisioned phones." }
        numbers: { type: array, in: body, description: "Only events of these numbers (strings)." }
      # No retry_on: a retried PUT could register the webhook twice.
      errors:
        format: json
        message_path: "$.error"
        terminal: [400, 401, 403, 404, 409, 422, 429, 502, 503, 504]
      pagination: none

    delete_subscription:
      method: DELETE
      path: /subscriptions/{id}
      access: dangerous
      description: "Remove a webhook subscription. Returns no body (204)."
      params:
        id: { type: string, in: path, required: true, description: "Subscription ID, e.g. sub-112ba1." }
      pagination: none

    # ── Microsoft Teams (direct routing) ───────────────────────────────────

    get_teams_integration:
      method: GET
      path: /microsoft_teams/integration
      access: read
      description: "The account's Microsoft Teams integration: {tenant_id, sbc_voice_routes, sync_status, available_ms_teams_seats, created_at}. Answers 403 until the Teams integration is enabled for API access."
      pagination: none

    list_teams_users:
      method: GET
      path: /microsoft_teams/users
      access: read
      description: "Microsoft Teams users imported to Placetel: {sip_user_id, ms_uuid, callerid, name, email, phone_system_enabled, resource_account (true = call queue account), account_enabled, sync_status, error_message}. Paged: plain array."
      params:
        "filter[sync_status]": { type: string, in: query, description: "not_synced, synced, syncing, sync_failed or disconnect_failed." }
        page: *p-page
        per_page: *p-per-page

    import_teams_user:
      method: POST
      path: /microsoft_teams/users
      access: write
      description: "Link a Microsoft Teams user to a Placetel SIP user (uses one booked Teams seat). The user needs a Microsoft 365 Phone System license. Returns the MsUser. Not retried automatically."
      params:
        sip_user_id: { type: integer, in: body, required: true, description: "SIP user ID." }
        ms_uuid: { type: string, in: body, required: true, description: "Microsoft user object ID (UUID)." }
      pagination: none

    sync_teams_user:
      method: PATCH
      path: /microsoft_teams/sync/{sip_user_id}
      access: write
      description: "Push the calling configuration of an imported user to Microsoft again. Returns the MsUser."
      params:
        sip_user_id: { type: integer, in: path, required: true, description: "SIP user ID." }
      pagination: none

    disconnect_teams_user:
      method: DELETE
      path: /microsoft_teams/users/{sip_user_id}
      access: dangerous
      description: "Disconnect an imported Teams user and sync that to Microsoft; the user loses Placetel calling in Teams. Returns no body (204)."
      params:
        sip_user_id: { type: integer, in: path, required: true, description: "SIP user ID." }
      pagination: none

    # ── Webex (Webex Calling wholesale) ────────────────────────────────────

    list_webex_users:
      method: GET
      path: /webex/users
      access: read
      description: "Users of the account for Webex: {id, login, first_name, last_name, webex_person_id, webex_subscriber_id, webex_subscriber_status, package, created_at, updated_at}. Without Webex the API answers 403 'Not available for your product'. Paged: plain array."
      params:
        "filter[first_name]": { type: string, in: query }
        "filter[last_name]": { type: string, in: query }
        "filter[login]": { type: string, in: query }
        page: *p-page
        per_page: *p-per-page

    create_webex_user:
      method: POST
      path: /webex/users
      access: admin
      description: "Create a user, optionally with a Webex license (package); licenses may be billed. Returns the WebexUser. Not retried automatically."
      params:
        first_name: { type: string, in: body, required: true }
        last_name: { type: string, in: body, required: true }
        email: { type: string, in: body, required: true, description: "E-mail address, used as login." }
        package: { type: string, in: body, description: "voice, meetings, calling, suite or cx_essentials." }
        location_id: { type: string, in: body, description: "Webex location ID." }
        phone_number: { type: string, in: body, description: "Primary phone number (E.164)." }
        extension: { type: string, in: body, description: "Calling extension." }
      pagination: none

    delete_webex_user:
      method: DELETE
      path: /webex/users/{id}
      access: dangerous
      description: "Delete a user and its Webex person. Irreversible. Returns no body (204)."
      params:
        id: { type: integer, in: path, required: true, description: "User ID from list_webex_users." }
      pagination: none

    get_webex_user_license:
      method: GET
      path: /webex/users/{id}/license
      access: read
      description: "The Webex license of a user: {package, change_package_to, change_package_at (scheduled change), canceled_at}."
      params:
        id: { type: integer, in: path, required: true, description: "User ID." }
      pagination: none

    assign_webex_user_license:
      method: POST
      path: /webex/users/{id}/license
      access: admin
      description: "Assign a Webex license to a user (may be billed). location_id, phone_number and extension only apply when the user has no license yet. Returns the License. Not retried automatically."
      params:
        id: { type: integer, in: path, required: true, description: "User ID." }
        package: { type: string, in: body, required: true, description: "voice, meetings, calling, suite or cx_essentials." }
        location_id: { type: string, in: body }
        phone_number: { type: string, in: body, description: "Primary phone number (E.164)." }
        extension: { type: string, in: body }
      pagination: none

    update_webex_user_license:
      method: PATCH
      path: /webex/users/{id}/license
      access: admin
      description: "Change the package of a user's Webex license; the change may be scheduled (see change_package_to and change_package_at in the result). Returns the License."
      params:
        id: { type: integer, in: path, required: true, description: "User ID." }
        package: { type: string, in: body, required: true, description: "voice, meetings, calling, suite or cx_essentials." }
      pagination: none

    list_webex_user_numbers:
      method: GET
      path: /webex/users/{id}/numbers
      access: read
      description: "Numbers configured for a Webex user (Number objects). Paged: plain array."
      params:
        id: { type: integer, in: path, required: true, description: "User ID." }
        page: *p-page
        per_page: *p-per-page

    update_webex_user_numbers:
      method: PATCH
      path: /webex/users/{id}/numbers
      access: write
      description: "Change the numbers of a Webex user. Returns the resulting numbers {primary, external, extension}."
      params:
        id: { type: integer, in: path, required: true, description: "User ID." }
        numbers: { type: array, in: body, description: "[{action (e.g. ADD, required), external (E.164), extension, primary (boolean, required), ring_pattern}]." }
      pagination: none

    list_webex_workspaces:
      method: GET
      path: /webex/workspaces
      access: read
      description: "Webex workspaces (rooms and shared devices): {id, display_name, supported_devices, capacity, type, calling}."
      params:
        display_name: { type: string, in: query, description: "Filter by display name." }
      pagination: none

    get_webex_workspace:
      method: GET
      path: /webex/workspaces/{id}
      access: read
      description: "One Webex workspace by ID."
      params:
        id: { type: integer, in: path, required: true, description: "Workspace ID." }
      pagination: none

    create_webex_workspace:
      method: POST
      path: /webex/workspaces
      access: write
      description: "Create a Webex workspace. Returns the Workspace. Not retried automatically."
      params:
        display_name: { type: string, in: body, required: true }
        supported_devices: { type: string, in: body, required: true, description: "phones or collaborationDevices." }
        calling: { type: string, in: body, required: true, description: "webexCalling, freeCalling or none." }
        location_id: { type: string, in: body, required: true, description: "Webex location ID." }
        phone_number: { type: string, in: body, description: "Phone number (E.164)." }
        extension: { type: string, in: body }
      pagination: none

    get_webex_fax_settings:
      method: GET
      path: /webex/numbers/{number_or_id}/fax_settings
      access: read
      description: "Fax settings of a Webex number: {routing_id, number, e164, faxheader, faxwhitelist, email, faxsettings, fax_attachment, webex_room_ids, license_id, license_package}. faxpin is masked."
      params:
        number_or_id: { type: string, in: path, required: true, description: "Phone number or number ID." }
      response:
        result_path: "$"
        redact: *redact-fax-settings
      pagination: none

    set_webex_fax_settings:
      method: PUT
      path: /webex/numbers/{number_or_id}/fax_settings
      access: admin
      description: "Turn a Webex number into a fax number or change its fax settings; provisions a fax license on the fly when none is free (may be billed). Returns the settings with faxpin masked."
      params:
        number_or_id: { type: string, in: path, required: true, description: "Phone number or number ID." }
        faxpin: { type: string, in: body, required: true, description: "Fax PIN, at least 4 digits." }
        faxheader: { type: string, in: body, required: true, description: "Fax header line." }
        faxwhitelist: { type: string, in: body, description: "Allowed sender addresses, comma or newline separated. Required unless the account has a verified customer domain linked to this number." }
        email: { type: string, in: body, description: "Recipient address for incoming faxes." }
        faxsettings: { type: integer, in: body, description: "E-mail routing setting (global vs. local)." }
        fax_attachment: { type: boolean, in: body, description: "Attach the fax as PDF." }
        webex_room_ids: { type: array, in: body, description: "Webex bot room IDs (integers) to notify." }
      response:
        result_path: "$"
        redact: *redact-fax-settings
      pagination: none

    delete_webex_fax_settings:
      method: DELETE
      path: /webex/numbers/{number_or_id}/fax_settings
      access: dangerous
      description: "Turn a fax number back into a regular number and free its fax license. Returns no body (204)."
      params:
        number_or_id: { type: string, in: path, required: true, description: "Phone number or number ID." }
      pagination: none

    # ── Customers (partner accounts only) ──────────────────────────────────

    list_customers:
      method: GET
      path: /customers
      access: read
      description: "Customers of a partner account, newest first: {id, customer_ref, login, first_name, last_name, company, country, product, status (test_phase | active | locked), created_at}. Only for partner accounts with a token that has the read:customers scope (403 otherwise). Paged: plain array."
      params:
        page: *p-page
        per_page: *p-per-page

    get_customer:
      method: GET
      path: /customers/{id}
      access: read
      description: "One customer of the partner account by ID (needs the read:customers scope)."
      params:
        id: { type: string, in: path, required: true, description: "Customer ID." }
      pagination: none

    create_customer:
      method: POST
      path: /customers
      access: admin
      description: >
        Create a customer account under the partner account. product must
        be one the partner may sell (the partner's default product when
        omitted); the address country must be one the partner may create
        customers in. Needs a partner token with customer scopes. Returns
        the new account. Not retried automatically.
      params:
        login: { type: string, in: body, required: true, description: "E-mail address the customer signs in with." }
        first_name: { type: string, in: body, required: true }
        last_name: { type: string, in: body, required: true }
        address_attributes: { type: object, in: body, required: true, description: "{first_name, last_name, company, street, streetno, zip, city, country, phonenumber (all required), street2, state, vat_number}." }
        locale: { type: string, in: body, description: "UI language: de, en, en-GB, en-US, fr, es or it." }
        product: { type: string, in: body, description: "Technical product name." }
        client_attributes: { type: object, in: body, description: "{source_country, current_num_extensions}." }
      pagination: none

  composites:
    summarize_calls:
      description: >
        Summarize the incoming call log of one day: totals per type
        (accepted, missed, voicemail, blocked), unread count, calls per
        dialed number, and the list of missed calls and voicemails with
        caller, matched contact name and time. Pages through list_calls (100
        per page, at most max_pages pages); truncated=true means the day had
        more calls than were read.
      access: read
      timeout: 60s
      depends_on: [list_calls]
      params:
        date:
          type: string
          description: "Day as YYYY-MM-DD. Defaults to today."
        max_pages:
          type: integer
          default: 10
          description: "Upper bound of pages read (100 calls each), at most 40."
      code: |
        const maxPages = Math.min(Math.max(params.max_pages || 10, 1), 40);
        const query = { per_page: 100 };
        if (params.date) query["filter[date]"] = params.date;
        const calls = [];
        let truncated = false;
        for (let page = 1; page <= maxPages; page++) {
          const batch = await api.list_calls(Object.assign({}, query, { page }));
          const items = Array.isArray(batch) ? batch : [];
          calls.push(...items);
          if (items.length < 100) break;
          if (page === maxPages) truncated = true;
        }
        const dialed = (c) => {
          const t = c.to_number;
          if (t == null) return "unknown";
          if (typeof t === "string") return t;
          const n = t.number;
          if (typeof n === "string") return n;
          if (n && typeof n === "object") return n.number || n.e164 || String(n.id);
          return t.e164 || "unknown";
        };
        const contactName = (c) => {
          const k = c.contact;
          if (!k) return null;
          const name = [k.first_name, k.last_name].filter(Boolean).join(" ");
          return name || k.company || null;
        };
        const byType = {};
        const byNumber = {};
        let unread = 0;
        const missed = [];
        for (const c of calls) {
          byType[c.type] = (byType[c.type] || 0) + 1;
          const d = dialed(c);
          byNumber[d] = (byNumber[d] || 0) + 1;
          if (c.unread) unread++;
          if (c.type === "missed" || c.type === "voicemail") {
            missed.push({
              id: c.id,
              type: c.type,
              from: c.from_number,
              contact: contactName(c),
              to: d,
              received_at: c.received_at,
              voicemail_url: c.type === "voicemail" ? c.file_url : undefined,
            });
          }
        }
        return {
          date: params.date || "today",
          total: calls.length,
          truncated,
          by_type: byType,
          unread,
          by_dialed_number: byNumber,
          missed_and_voicemail: missed,
        };

  examples:
    - name: "Missed calls today with caller names"
      description: "List today's missed calls and voicemails with the matched contact."
      code: |
        const calls = await api.list_calls({ "filter[type]": "voicemail,missed", per_page: 100 });
        return calls.map(c => ({
          from: c.from_number,
          who: c.contact ? [c.contact.first_name, c.contact.last_name].filter(Boolean).join(" ") || c.contact.company : null,
          type: c.type,
          at: c.received_at,
        }));
    - name: "Caller lookup"
      description: "Find the contact behind a phone number."
      code: |
        const hits = await api.list_contacts({ "search[number]": "02211234567" });
        return hits.map(c => ({ id: c.id, name: `${c.first_name || ""} ${c.last_name || ""}`.trim(), company: c.company }));
    - name: "Click-to-dial"
      description: "Ring the extension of a SIP user, then connect it to an external number."
      code: |
        const users = await api.list_sip_users({ "filter[did]": 23 });
        if (users.length === 0) return "no SIP user with extension 23";
        return await api.initiate_call({ sipuid: users[0].sipuid, target: "+492211234567" });
    - name: "Forward a number to a mobile phone"
      description: "Ring the office extension for 20 seconds, then a mobile phone, then the mailbox."
      code: |
        const office = (await api.list_sip_users({ "filter[did]": 23 }))[0];
        return await api.update_routing({
          number_or_id: "02211234567",
          forward: {
            destinations: [
              { targets: [office.sipuid], ringing_time: 20 },
              { targets: ["+491701234567"], ringing_time: 30 },
            ],
            behaviour: "mailbox",
          },
        });
